Modifications by Provable Games, based on upstream commit
3d75aee4b3f43cbd932265e7d60201fd5b770397:

  - webaudio-tinysynth.js: removed the GUI panel (canvas display,
    play/seek/volume controls, MIDI file drag-and-drop) and the
    <webaudio-tinysynth> custom element. The WebAudioTinySynth
    JavaScript API is unchanged.
  - webaudio-tinysynth.js: loadMIDI keeps the tempo from MIDI tempo
    events (microseconds per quarter note) as a fractional BPM instead
    of rounding it down to a whole number, so songs play at their exact
    tempo.
  - webaudio-tinysynth.js: added the loopEnd property and setLoopEnd()
    so a looping song can restart on a bar boundary instead of on its
    last event. With loopEnd unset (0) behavior is unchanged.
  - webaudio-tinysynth.js: loadMIDI parses Standard MIDI Files with
    bounded, validated reads. Malformed or unsupported input (format 2,
    SMPTE or zero division, truncation) throws an Error with a code
    (SMF_*) and keeps the previous song.
  - webaudio-tinysynth.js: the sequencer handles at most 1000 events
    per timer callback, and a looping song whose events all share one
    tick ends after one pass instead of hanging. A song with no events
    other than tempo stays stopped. locateMIDI() rebuilds the song's
    tempo and channel state from the start without keeping earlier
    overrides, and replaying a completed song restarts from its initial
    tempo and channel state.
  - webaudio-tinysynth.js: added resume(), dispose() and the constructor
    options context, destination and lazy. dispose() stops and
    disconnects every voice and node, clears the timers and closes only
    a context the synth created; setAudioContext() tears down the
    previous graph the same way. stopMIDI() now also stops drums and
    queued controller changes (seeks too; loading a song keeps the
    upstream calls). Ended voices are disconnected, send() no longer
    leaves unhandled rejections, and on an OfflineAudioContext the
    timer leaves scheduled notes alone and playMIDI() throws
    AUDIO_CONTEXT_OFFLINE.
  - webaudio-tinysynth.js: with loopEnd set, the first pass of a song
    started from tick 0 keeps the rest before its first event, as later
    passes already did, and getPlayStatus() has a startTime: the
    AudioContext time at which tick 0 of the current pass sounds.
  - webaudio-tinysynth.js: added setSampleWave() and setHarmonicWave(),
    a registry of custom single-cycle and harmonic waveforms that
    timbres reference by name. Sample tables are held to a home pitch
    near 440 Hz and keep their own pitch basis; registered waves survive
    setQuality() and context changes. setTimbre() rejects unknown wave
    names.
  - webaudio-tinysynth.js: added optional fixed operator filters (timbre
    fields fl, ff, fq and fk): a BiquadFilterNode between an output
    operator's gain and its channel, key-trackable and clamped below
    Nyquist, released with its voice. setTimbre() rejects invalid filter
    fields before any change.
  - webaudio-tinysynth.js: the reverb impulse and the n0/n1 noise
    buffers are generated from seeded mulberry32 streams (one per
    buffer) instead of Math.random, with a fixed default seed of 0, a
    seed constructor option and read-only seed and bufferVersion
    properties. The generated reverb and noise texture differs from
    upstream once and is then the same on every load.
  - webaudio-tinysynth.js: public functions validate their arguments and
    timbres before changing anything (TypeError/RangeError), setTimbre()
    stores a validated copy instead of modifying the caller's objects,
    malformed raw MIDI messages are ignored, and loadMIDIUrl() returns a
    cancellable promise that rejects on HTTP, network and parse errors
    and ignores stale responses.
  - webaudio-tinysynth.js: a note whose computed AudioParam values are
    outside the 32-bit float range is skipped instead of throwing part-way
    through, setTimbre() bounds its time fields to that range, and
    timestamp mode 1 clamps converted times at the current time.
  - webaudio-tinysynth.min.js and its source map are regenerated from
    the modified source.
  - Demo pages and README updated to use the JavaScript API; tests added.
